[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. Its reports hold two problems, and the queued fix reaches only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close the reports in #4471 when the parser fix ships. The form hint needs its own fix, and its reports will continue until that fix ships.
</Callout>

## The two problems

<CauseTable ticket={4471} {filed} />

**`parser`:** The shared parser reads every date month first, so the dates of day-first tenants come out flipped. This reaches every tenant and every channel. [Ticket 1](https://github.com/HugoDulce/MegaDev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) tracks it.

**`hint`:** The `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, then reads the date day first. People type what the hint says, so their dates come out flipped too. Only form reports from day-first tenants on `booking-v3` have this cause. [Ticket 2](https://github.com/HugoDulce/MegaDev-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) tracks it.

## How to read the counts

- The table is computed when the page renders, by `causes.ts`. Do not retype its numbers.
- The cause comes from the tenant and the channel, not from `intakeTag`. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser, and the table shows how often it disagrees.
- The export repeats some reports, because its pages overlap. The table counts each id once.

## What is still unconfirmed

The one-day reports under the table do not look like a flip. A flip cannot turn 12 May into 11 May. The desk files them under `parser` by tenant, and this page keeps that rule, but nobody has confirmed their cause. Read them again after the parser fix ships. If they keep coming, they need their own ticket.

## Why one ticket hid this

Both problems produce the same complaint, so their subject lines match. [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone, and the [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) repeats that rule. A decision is never edited, so the desk needs a new record that replaces it: merge on cause, not on subject.

